From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:14:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] H1: build hayro-syntax pages lazily; add
 Page::from_dict

Pdf::new no longer walks the page tree. The pages are built on the first
call to Pdf::pages() and cached for the life of the Pdf, so opening a
large document costs only the xref (about 33 bytes per object retained
for a 100,000-page tree, against about 680 before) and the recursive
walk no longer runs at open.

New API for callers that walk the tree themselves:
- Pdf::pages_root(): the catalog's /Pages reference.
- Pdf::pages_built(): whether pages() has been called.
- Pdf::xref_was_repaired(): whether the xref table was rebuilt.
- page::InheritedAttributes and Page::from_dict(): build the same Page
  the eager walk yields, from the leaf dictionary and what it inherits.

Page::new becomes infallible; the brute-force /Contents check moves to
its only caller. Because the tree is no longer read at open, a /Pages
reference that does not resolve now opens with no pages instead of
failing with LoadPdfError::Invalid; a catalog without /Pages still fails.
